---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Operations Management & People Leadership" current="/operations-leadership/" description="Richard Allen's operations and people-leadership experience across SaaS support, workforce operations, reporting, process improvement, coaching, project coordination, and warehouse management.">
<section class="page-intro"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">Operations Management & People Leadership</div><h1>Build structure around people, priorities, workflows, data, and change.</h1><p class="lede">My operations experience spans team leadership, workflow coordination, reporting, coaching, process improvement, service delivery, cross-functional work, and earlier warehouse and supply operations.</p></div></section>

<section class="section impact-section"><div class="container">
  <div class="stats-grid compact-stats">
    <article class="stat-card teal"><div class="stat-orbit"><span class="metric">10+</span></div><div class="metric-label">support professionals led and coached in day-to-day operations</div></article>
    <article class="stat-card blue"><div class="stat-orbit"><span class="metric">400+</span></div><div class="metric-label">position records managed across multiple OHA divisions</div></article>
    <article class="stat-card gold"><div class="stat-orbit"><span class="metric">20+</span></div><div class="metric-label">recurring and ad-hoc workforce reports maintained for leadership</div></article>
    <article class="stat-card violet"><div class="stat-orbit"><span class="metric">16+</span></div><div class="metric-label">warehouse staff managed in earlier Aramark operations leadership</div></article>
  </div>
  <div class="operating-model" aria-label="Operations leadership model">
    <div><span class="model-dot teal-dot"></span><strong>People</strong><small>Coach, communicate, develop</small></div>
    <div><span class="model-arrow">→</span></div>
    <div><span class="model-dot blue-dot"></span><strong>Workflow</strong><small>Clarify priorities and coverage</small></div>
    <div><span class="model-arrow">→</span></div>
    <div><span class="model-dot gold-dot"></span><strong>Measures</strong><small>Make work visible through reporting</small></div>
    <div><span class="model-arrow">→</span></div>
    <div><span class="model-dot violet-dot"></span><strong>Improve</strong><small>Fix friction and reinforce better ways of working</small></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section"><div class="container">
  <div class="section-heading-row"><div><div class="eyebrow">Operations in practice</div><h2>Leadership with the operating system attached.</h2></div><p class="section-note">Not just supervising people—also improving the information, procedures, coordination, and routines around the work.</p></div>
  <div class="grid two value-grid">
    <article class="card accent-teal"><div class="card-icon">LEAD</div><h3>Support-team leadership</h3><p>At HawkSoft, led and coached a 10+ person customer and technical-support team. Work included hiring-team participation, performance-evaluation support, quality review, workflow coverage, escalations, stand-ups, and one-on-one coaching.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-blue"><div class="card-icon">FLOW</div><h3>Service workflow & coordination</h3><p>Monitored support coverage, escalations, team activity, and service needs while coordinating with development and other teams around releases, troubleshooting, customer migrations, and operational priorities.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-gold"><div class="card-icon">DATA</div><h3>Management reporting</h3><p>Analyzed support and phone-system data in Excel, using pivots and KPI-style reporting to turn large raw exports into information leadership could use for decisions and follow-up.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-violet"><div class="card-icon">400+</div><h3>Workforce operations at scale</h3><p>As Position Manager / Operations & Policy Analyst II at Oregon Health Authority, managed 400+ position records, organizational charts, vacancy and position trackers, and 20+ recurring or ad-hoc workforce reports.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-blue"><div class="card-icon">X-FN</div><h3>Cross-functional coordination</h3><p>At OHA, coordinated with Recruiting, HR, Classification & Compensation, Budget, DEI, and leadership. At HawkSoft and The Kotter Group, work repeatedly connected customer-facing teams, software, training, documentation, and operations.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-teal"><div class="card-icon">OPS</div><h3>Administrative operations</h3><p>At Marion County Health & Human Services, coordinated scheduling, intake, service coordination, reporting and data accuracy, onboarding, cross-training, and multiple competing priorities in a confidential environment.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-gold"><div class="card-icon">SOP</div><h3>Process governance & consistency</h3><p>At Oregon Employment Department, led and revamped a multi-month SOP initiative encompassing 100+ procedures while supporting documentation, training, staff communication, modernization, and continuous-improvement work.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-violet"><div class="card-icon">16+</div><h3>Warehouse & supply operations</h3><p>Earlier at Aramark Foodservice, managed a warehouse team of 16+ and six-figure weekly inventory while overseeing procurement, receiving, storage, distribution, shipping, sanitation, and driver or small-fleet activity.</p></article>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section tight"><div class="container"><div class="callout"><strong>Leadership style:</strong> create clarity, make work visible, coach people toward stronger performance, and improve the system around them so good work is easier to repeat.</div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
